{
  "dom_id": "step-e13932",
  "name": "Example: Solving Compound Inequalities",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $0 \\leq 3x+6 < 15.$",
  "worked_solution": "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t0 &\\leq 3x+6 < 15 \\[5pt]\n\t0 - 6 &\\leq 3x + 6 -6 < 15-6 \\[5pt]\n\t-6 &\\leq 3x < 9 \\[5pt]\n\t\\dfrac{-6}{3} &\\leq \\dfrac{3x}{3} < \\dfrac{9}{3} \\[5pt]\n\t-2 &\\leq x < 3\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2 \\leq x < 3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
